# Book :1060 ("Positional actual arguments precede named ones"): a call's actuals are bound to its callee's
# formals -- by position, then by name; a named argument's body is its formal's value.  f(a: 8; b: 1),
# f(b: 1; a: 8), f(8; b: 1), f(a: x; b: 0 + 1), from method g f(b: 1; a: 8), and a call bound inside an
# argument, f(b: 1; a: f(b: 1; a: 9)), are all 7.  Before,
# a named argument was read as a call of its name: "unknown method".  Entry 7.
fn: f (int: a; int: b) int
    return: a - b
fn: g () int
    int: t 0
    t: f(b: 1; a: 8)
    return: t
int: x 8
int: r1 0
int: r2 0
int: r3 0
int: r4 0
int: r5 0
int: r6 0
r1: f(a: 8; b: 1)
r2: f(b: 1; a: 8)
r3: f(8; b: 1)
r4: f(a: x; b: 0 + 1)
r5: g()
r6: f(b: 1; a: f(b: 1; a: 9))
if: r1 != 7
    sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 81; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
    return
if: r2 != 7
    sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 82; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
    return
if: r3 != 7
    sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 83; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
    return
if: r4 != 7
    sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 84; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
    return
if: r5 != 7
    sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 85; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
    return
if: r6 != 7
    sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 86; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
    return
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 7; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
